Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The full inventory of bundled tools, datasets and their terms is maintained in
docs/third-party.md. That page is authoritative for what a given image actually
contains; this file records the attributions that must travel with the source
and with every image built from it.

EPSS data
---------

This product includes Exploit Prediction Scoring System (EPSS) data provided by
FIRST.org, used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Source: https://www.first.org/epss/
Bundled at: scanner/data/epss/epss-overlay.json

The data is redistributed as part of this repository and is baked into the
published images as the seed set, so this attribution applies to both. No
endorsement by FIRST.org is implied.

CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities and NVD CVSS v4 data
---------------------------------------------------------

Works of the United States government, in the public domain. Bundled at
scanner/data/kev/ and scanner/data/cvss4/. No attribution is required; the
sources are named in docs/third-party.md for provenance.

Exploit maturity data
---------------------

Derived from Exploit-DB (GPL-2.0) and the Metasploit Framework (BSD-3-Clause).
Only CVE identifiers and a maturity rung are extracted — no exploit code,
titles or descriptions are copied. See docs/third-party.md for the reasoning.

Public Suffix List
------------------

This product includes the Public Suffix List (https://publicsuffix.org/),
subject to the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/).
It is bundled unmodified, licence header included, at
scanner/pipeline/public_suffix_list.dat; that file is its own source form.

Subdomain-takeover catalogue
----------------------------

scanner/pipeline/takeover_fingerprints.json contains takeover statuses and
fingerprint strings adapted from "can-i-take-over-xyz" by EdOverflow and
contributors (https://github.com/EdOverflow/can-i-take-over-xyz), used under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: a selection of entries, re-expressed as a JSON catalogue with this
project's own CNAME patterns, notes and identifiers; some fingerprints replaced
with ones from ProjectDiscovery's nuclei-templates (MIT,
https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates). No endorsement by the
authors is implied.

Rhai plugins derived from GenDec
--------------------------------

Three of the Rhai plugins in scanner/pipeline/pulse_data/plugins/ are adapted from
scripts of GenDec (the Pulse scanner, https://github.com/onixus/GenDec, release
v1.3.0, licensed MIT per its Cargo.toml `license` field):

  shapo_ssh_banner.rhai             from scripts/ssh_audit.rhai
  shapo_smb_exposure.rhai           from scripts/smb_netbios_exposure_audit.rhai
  shapo_remote_admin_exposure.rhai  from scripts/rdp_vnc_exposure_audit.rhai

Each file keeps an SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT header that names its origin and
lists what was changed. The MIT licence permits use, modification and
redistribution provided its copyright and permission notice are kept with the
copies; the notice of the GenDec release applies to these three files. The other
plugins in that directory are original to this project (Apache-2.0).

LGPL components
---------------

The published images include fpdf2 and psycopg, both LGPL-3.0-only, used as
unmodified libraries through their public Python interfaces. Their source is
available from the Python Package Index at the versions pinned in
requirements.txt and requirements-api.txt, and either may be replaced with a
compatible version by reinstalling it in the image.

Nmap
----

The images contain no Nmap, nmap-vulners or Vulscan. Releases up to and
including 0.47-1009-rc1 published an opt-in "-nmap" image tag that did; later
releases do not. Users who install Nmap (Nmap Public Source License) next to
the sensor, or in an image of their own, are responsible for the obligations
that licence carries, including its restrictions on commercial and OEM
redistribution. See docs/nmap-external.md and docs/third-party.md.
